-- AN INSTRUMENT, NOT ADVICE. Four duration binds, all reading ARDENT DEFENDER's cooldown
-- (31850, ~90s, self-cast, no target, castable out of combat) and glowing four other icons.
-- Subject and bound spell are independent, so one press lights a ladder somewhere else.
--
-- ANSWERED: the input is SECONDS. This ladder flew and the crossing was seen -- the `> 30s`
-- mark went dark at thirty seconds remaining on a ~90s cooldown, with `> 0.5s` and `< 1000s`
-- lit and `> 1000s` dark throughout, and every mark dark both before the cast and after the
-- cooldown ended. A millisecond domain would have dropped `> 30s` at 30ms and a [0, 1] one
-- would never have lit it, so the reading separates all three. It also shows the curve TRACKS
-- rather than evaluating once.
--
-- The ladder is kept as the instrument that settled it, and is the thing to re-fly if a patch
-- makes a duration bind start reading wrong. The question it was built for -- `Duration.lua`
-- writes the rule's seconds straight in as a curve point, and the sibling health curve turned
-- out to take [0, 1] where "percent" was assumed, costing four releases of silently dark
-- health binds -- is closed.
--
-- Right after casting, remaining is ~90 seconds. So the input is ~90 on a seconds domain,
-- ~90000 on milliseconds, ~1.0 on a [0, 1] fraction. Points at 30 and 1000 straddle all three.
--
-- Read it as a decision tree, not a count:
--
--   Consecration and Avenger's Shield are exact complements -- which is lit is the answer:
--     Avenger's Shield lit      input is seconds or a fraction
--     Consecration lit          input is MILLISECONDS
--
--   Shield of the Righteous then separates the remaining pair:
--     lit                       input is SECONDS -- the shipped assumption holds
--     dark                      input is a [0, 1] FRACTION
--
--   Word of Glory dark while a cooldown is running means nothing drives alpha at all, and
--   the other three say nothing.
--
-- On the flight, Avenger's Shield and Shield of the Righteous both lit: seconds.
--
-- `< 1000s` carries `absent dark` because `<` on a cooldown is also true at zero remaining,
-- which would glow permanently while the spell is up.
--
-- Check it, or turn it into a share string:
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo check  projects/smart-glo/rules/protection-durationprobe.sg
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo encode projects/smart-glo/rules/protection-durationprobe.sg

spec paladin.protection

glow "DPROBE: Ardent Defender cooldown > 0.5s (anything at all)"
  on     word_of_glory
  bind   31850.cooldown > 0.5s

glow "DPROBE: > 30s (lit on seconds or ms, dark on a fraction)"
  on     shield_of_the_righteous
  bind   31850.cooldown > 30s

glow "DPROBE: > 1000s (lit ONLY on milliseconds)"
  on     consecration
  bind   31850.cooldown > 1000s

glow "DPROBE: < 1000s (complement of the rung above)"
  on     avengers_shield
  bind   31850.cooldown < 1000s absent dark

-- The `outside` form: the only compile shape with two transitions, and it has never run.
-- One press shows all three edges on this one icon -- lit from the cast down to 60s, dark
-- through 60..30, lit again under 30, then dark when the spell comes up.
glow "DPROBE: outside 30s..60s (three edges on one icon)"
  on     divine_toll
  bind   31850.cooldown outside 30s..60s absent dark
